00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
The auxiliary vertex receives and sends the same number of arcs.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Pairing each incoming arc with its own return creates three isolated loops.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Cross the pairings to join two components while preserving all degrees.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
One more switch produces a directed cycle on the original vertices.
